== Mock Examination 1 — Questions

#mcq(1, [The industrial importance of cracking is that it], [produces only carbon dioxide], [removes water from the oil], [makes the oil heavier], [matches the supply of fractions to the demand for them])

#mcq(2, [Which of the following gases will NOT decolourise bromine water?], [ethene], [ethyne], [ethane], [propene])

#mcq(3, [The volume of 0.100 mol dm⁻³ sodium hydroxide needed to neutralise 25.0 cm³ of 0.200 mol dm⁻³ ethanoic acid is], [12.5 cm³], [50.0 cm³], [25.0 cm³], [100 cm³])

#mcq(4, [Which of these statements about PET is correct?], [It is a condensation polymer of a diol and a diacid], [It is an addition polymer of ethene], [It is a natural polymer], [It contains no oxygen])

#mcq(5, [The white of an egg turns opaque when boiled because], [the water evaporates], [the protein is hydrolysed], [the fat melts], [the protein is denatured and becomes insoluble])

#mcq(6, [Which of these would be used to make up 250 cm³ of a standard solution?], [a 250 cm³ beaker], [a 250 cm³ volumetric flask], [a 250 cm³ measuring cylinder], [a conical flask])

#mcq(7, [When 1 mol of an alkane is burnt completely, 4 mol of carbon dioxide and 5 mol of water are produced. The alkane is], [pentane], [hexane], [butane], [propane])

#mcq(8, [Ethene is stored and transported under pressure because], [it is a gas at room temperature with a low boiling point], [it is a solid], [it reacts with air], [it is a liquid])

#mcq(9, [Which reagent would give a positive test with ethanoic acid but not with ethanol?], [sodium metal], [bromine water], [litmus paper], [sodium carbonate solution])

#mcq(10, [A fat is boiled with sodium hydroxide and the product is acidified. The substance obtained is], [soap], [a fatty acid], [glycerol], [an ester])

#mcq(11, [Which of these will NOT give a violet colour with Biuret reagent?], [egg albumen], [milk], [glucose solution], [gelatin])

#mcq(12, [In paper chromatography the solvent front is], [the furthest point reached by the solvent], [the line where the spots were placed], [the top edge of the paper], [the position of the most soluble dye])

#mcq(13, [The alkane with nine carbon atoms has the formula], [C₉H₁₈], [C₉H₂₂], [C₉H₁₆], [C₉H₂₀])

#mcq(14, [The compound CH₂=CHCH₂CH₃ is], [but-1-ene], [but-2-ene], [2-methylpropene], [butane])

#mcq(15, [The product of the dehydration of propan-2-ol is], [propane], [propene], [propanone], [propanoic acid])

#mcq(16, [A poly(ethene) sample has a relative molecular mass of 56 000. Its degree of polymerisation is], [1 000], [4 000], [2 000], [5 600])

#mcq(17, [Heavy-metal ions such as Pb²⁺ and Hg²⁺ are poisonous because they], [are radioactive], [denature proteins by binding to –SH and other groups], [react with water], [are acids])

#mcq(18, [Concentrated sulphuric acid is used to dry], [carbon dioxide], [ammonia], [hydrogen sulphide], [ammonia and hydrogen])

#mcq(19, [The number of moles of oxygen needed to burn 1 mol of propane completely is], [3], [4], [5], [7])

#mcq(20, [Which of these statements about alkenes and alkanes is TRUE?], [Alkenes are saturated], [Alkanes decolourise bromine water], [Alkanes add hydrogen across a double bond], [Alkenes burn in air])

#mcq(21, [Which of these is the correct ionic equation for the ionisation of ethanoic acid?], [CH₃COOH ⇌ CH₃COO⁻ + H⁺], [CH₃COOH → CH₃COO⁻ + H⁺], [CH₃COOH + H₂O → CH₃COO⁻ + H₃O⁺ completely], [CH₃COOH → CH₄ + CO₂])

#mcq(22, [Sodium chloride is added to the soap mixture in order to], [make the soap harder], [precipitate the soap so that it can be separated], [neutralise the alkali], [dissolve the glycerol])

#mcq(23, [Which of these is a test for water?], [Benedict's solution], [iodine solution], [anhydrous copper(II) sulphate], [limewater])

#mcq(24, [Constant mass is used in a gravimetric experiment to ensure that], [the sample is pure], [the balance is accurate], [the sample is dry], [all the water or gas has been driven off])

#mcq(25, [Which of the following equations represents incomplete combustion?], [CH₄ + 2O₂ → CO₂ + 2H₂O], [C₂H₆ + 3½O₂ → 2CO₂ + 3H₂O], [2CH₄ + 3O₂ → 2CO + 4H₂O], [C₃H₈ + 5O₂ → 3CO₂ + 4H₂O])

#mcq(26, [Which pair will react together?], [ethene and water, in the dark, with no catalyst], [ethane and bromine in the dark], [ethane and bromine water], [ethene and bromine in the dark])

#mcq(27, [Which of these statements about ethanol is FALSE?], [It is a strong electrolyte], [It is miscible with water], [It is a good solvent for organic substances], [It burns with a clean flame])

#mcq(28, [The hardness of water is caused mainly by the ions], [Na⁺ and K⁺], [Ca²⁺ and Mg²⁺], [Cl⁻ and NO₃⁻], [H⁺ and OH⁻])

#mcq(29, [The protein content of a foodstuff containing 0.80 g of nitrogen in 25.0 g of sample is], [3.2 %], [16 %], [20 %], [5.0 %])

#mcq(30, [The separation of a mixture of sand and salt is carried out by], [adding water, filtering, then evaporating the filtrate], [heating the mixture], [using a magnet], [chromatography])

#mcq(31, [The reagent that would distinguish methane from ethene is], [water], [sodium chloride solution], [dilute sulphuric acid], [bromine water])

#mcq(32, [Ethene is described as planar because], [it is a gas], [the two carbons and four hydrogens lie in one plane], [it has a triple bond], [it is symmetrical])

#mcq(33, [Which of these reagents will convert ethanol to chloroethane?], [phosphorus(V) chloride], [chlorine in sunlight], [sodium chloride solution], [hydrogen chloride gas only])

#mcq(34, [Which of these is an advantage of soap over detergent?], [it lathers in hard water], [it contains phosphates], [it is readily biodegradable], [it is made from petroleum])

#mcq(35, [A polypeptide is formed by], [the hydrolysis of a protein], [the oxidation of an alcohol], [the addition of hydrogen to a fat], [the condensation of amino acids])

#mcq(36, [Why is dilute nitric acid added before silver nitrate in the halide test?], [to speed up the reaction], [to remove carbonate and sulphite ions that would also give a precipitate], [to dissolve the silver chloride], [to change the colour])

#mcq(37, [The alkane that is a liquid at room temperature is], [methane], [ethane], [propane], [decane])

#mcq(38, [The volume of hydrogen at s.t.p. required to convert 2.24 dm³ of ethene at s.t.p. into ethane is], [1.12 dm³], [2.24 dm³], [4.48 dm³], [22.4 dm³])

#mcq(39, [The property of ethanol that makes it useful in a spirit thermometer is its], [low freezing point and steady expansion], [high boiling point], [acidity], [colour])

#mcq(40, [The scum formed by soap in hard water is], [sodium stearate], [calcium carbonate], [calcium stearate], [magnesium sulphate])

